    </div>
    
    <p class="title is-5 mathjax">
      
        KP-<span class="search-hit mathjax">Agent</span>: Keyword Pruning in Sponsored Search Advertising via LLM-Powered Contextual Bandits
      
    </p>
    <p class="authors">
      <span class="has-text-black-bis has-text-weight-semibold">Authors:</span>
      
      <a href="/search/?searchtype=author&amp;query=Long%2C+H">Hou-Wan Long</a>, 
      
      <a href="/search/?searchtype=author&amp;query=Song%2C+Y">Yicheng Song</a>, 
      
      <a href="/search/?searchtype=author&amp;query=Wang%2C+Z">Zidong Wang</a>, 
      
      <a href="/search/?searchtype=author&amp;query=Sun%2C+T">Tianshu Sun</a>
      
    </p>
    
    <p class="abstract mathjax">
      <span class="has-text-black-bis has-text-weight-semibold">Abstract</span>:
      <span class="abstract-short has-text-grey-dark mathjax" id="2601.05257v1-abstract-short" style="display: inline;">
        Sponsored search advertising (SSA) requires advertisers to constantly adjust keyword strategies. While bid adjustment and keyword generation are well-studied, keyword pruning-refining keyword sets to enhance campaign performance-remains under-explored. This paper addresses critical inefficiencies in current practices as evidenced by a dataset containing 0.5 million SSA records from a pharmaceutica&hellip;
        <a class="is-size-7" style="white-space: nowrap;" onclick="document.getElementById('2601.05257v1-abstract-full').style.display = 'inline'; document.getElementById('2601.05257v1-abstract-short').style.display = 'none';">&#9661; More</a>
      </span>
      <span class="abstract-full has-text-grey-dark mathjax" id="2601.05257v1-abstract-full" style="display: none;">
        Sponsored search advertising (SSA) requires advertisers to constantly adjust keyword strategies. While bid adjustment and keyword generation are well-studied, keyword pruning-refining keyword sets to enhance campaign performance-remains under-explored. This paper addresses critical inefficiencies in current practices as evidenced by a dataset containing 0.5 million SSA records from a pharmaceutical advertiser on search engine Meituan, China&#39;s largest delivery platform. We propose KP-Agent, an LLM agentic system with domain tool set and a memory module. By modeling keyword pruning within a contextual bandit framework, KP-Agent generates code snippets to refine keyword sets through reinforcement learning. Experiments show KP-Agent improves cumulative profit by up to 49.28% over baselines.
        <a class="is-size-7" style="white-space: nowrap;" onclick="document.getElementById('2601.05257v1-abstract-full').style.display = 'none'; document.getElementById('2601.05257v1-abstract-short').style.display = 'inline';">&#9651; Less</a>
      </span>
    </p>
    

    <p class="is-size-7"><span class="has-text-black-bis has-text-weight-semibold">Submitted</span> 20 October, 2025; 
      <span class="has-text-black-bis has-text-weight-semibold">originally announced</span> January 2026.
      
    </p>
    

    

    
